@startuml
title 5G Architecture — NG-RAN + 5GC + IMS (Pure Class Diagram Style)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
left to right direction

' ============================================================
' UE + RAN
' ============================================================
package "UE" {
  class UE {
    + USIM
    + SUPI/SUCI
    + NAS Signaling
    + PDU Sessions
  }
}

package "NG-RAN (5G Radio Access Network)" {
  class gNB {
    + Radio scheduling
    + Handover
    + QoS flow mapping\n(QFI -> DRB)
    + Forwards NAS messages
  }
}

' ============================================================
' 5G Core Network Functions (5GC)
' ============================================================
package "5GC (5G Core)" {

  class AMF {
    + Control Plane entry
    + Registration
    + Mobility Management
    + NAS termination
    + Auth orchestration
  }

  class AUSF {
    + Authentication Server
    + Verifies RES*
    + Derives auth outputs
  }

  class UDM {
    + Subscriber DB
    + Subscription data
  }

  class ARPF {
    + Auth credential processing
    + Generates AV\n(RAND,AUTN,XRES*)
  }

  class SMF {
    + Session mgmt
    + Creates PDU session
    + Selects UPF
    + QoS rules for session
  }

  class UPF {
    + User Plane forwarding
    + Routing/traffic steering
    + QoS enforcement
    + Gateway to DN
  }

  class PCF {
    + Policy control
    + QoS/policy decisions
  }

  class NRF {
    + NF repository
    + Service discovery
    + Registry of NF endpoints
  }

  class NSSF {
    + Slice selection
    + Chooses S-NSSAI policy
  }
}

package "IMS (Voice Services: VoNR)" {
  class "P-CSCF" as PCSCF {
    + SIP Proxy
    + First IMS hop
  }

  class "S-CSCF" as SCSCF {
    + SIP Serving
    + Call control
  }

  class "IMS App Server" as IMSSRV {
    + TAS/AS logic
    + Supplementary services
  }
}

package "External Networks" {
  class "DN / Internet" as DN
  class "PSTN / Legacy Voice" as PSTN
}

' ============================================================
' Interfaces / Connections
' ============================================================

' UE <-> RAN
UE --> gNB : 5G NR Air\n(AS: RRC/PDCP/RLC/MAC/PHY)

' Control Plane path
gNB --> AMF : N2\n(Control Plane, NAS forwarding)

' User Plane path
gNB --> UPF : N3\n(GTP-U user data)

' UPF to Internet
UPF --> DN : N6\n(IP traffic)

' SMF configures UPF
SMF --> UPF : N4\n(PDR/FAR/QER rules)

' SBA Service-based interactions (HTTP/2 APIs)
AMF --> NRF : Discover NFs\n(service discovery)
SMF --> NRF : Discover NFs
AUSF --> NRF : Discover UDM

AMF --> AUSF : Nausf\n(UE Authentication)
AUSF --> UDM : Nudm\n(UE Auth Data)
UDM --> ARPF : Credential processing\n(generate auth vectors)

SMF --> PCF : Npcf\n(Session Policy)
AMF --> PCF : Npcf\n(Access/Mobility Policy)
AMF --> NSSF : Nnssf\n(Slice selection)

' Voice over NR uses IMS
UE --> PCSCF : SIP Signaling\n(VoNR)
PCSCF --> SCSCF : SIP core
SCSCF --> IMSSRV : Service triggers
IMSSRV --> PSTN : Interconnect\n(optional)

note bottom
Key Concepts:
- NAS is logically UE<->AMF (via gNB forwarding)
- Control Plane: N2 + SBA APIs (AMF/SMF/AUSF/UDM/PCF/NRF)
- User Plane: N3 (gNB<->UPF) and N6 (UPF<->Internet)
- UPF is data gateway; SMF programs UPF using N4.
- IMS supports voice: VoNR (or EPS fallback to VoLTE).
end note

@enduml
